  "description": "🚀 How to Use RS.Dapper.Utility in C# for Multi-Database Support 🚀\nIf you’re working with Dapper in C#, managing different databases like MS SQL Server, PostgreSQL, and MySQL can sometimes get tricky. But with RS.Dapper.Utility, switching between these databases is super simple — just update your appsettings.json and you’re good to go!\n✨ Why RS.Dapper.Utility?\nSupports MS SQL Server, PostgreSQL & MySQL with minimal config\nSimplifies CRUD operations with dynamic SQL generation\nEnsures secure, parameterized queries\nIntegrates seamlessly with your existing projects",
